"""Build a reviewable calf free-body audit; preserve uncertainty explicitly."""
import json,html
from pathlib import Path
from jump_rig import ROOT

def main():
    out=ROOT/'results/jump_contact_visualization'
    audit=json.loads((ROOT/'results/contact_jump_scapula/600hz/calf_moment_audit.json').read_text())
    quality=json.loads((ROOT/'results/contact_jump_scapula/600hz/motion_quality.json').read_text())
    validation=json.loads((out/'validation.json').read_text())
    rows=[]
    for a in audit['audits']:
        rows.append('<tr>'+''.join(f'<td>{v}</td>' for v in [a['side'].upper(),f"{a['time_s']:.3f}",f"{a['same_foot_GRF_N'][2]:.0f}",f"{a['effective_external_lever_m']*100:.1f}",f"{a['required_net_ankle_moment_Nm']:.1f}",f"{a['calf_muscle_moment_Nm']:.1f}",f"{a['force_weighted_calf_moment_arm_m']*100:.2f}",f"{a['total_calf_elements_tension_N']:.0f}"] )+'</tr>')
    q=quality['checks']; significant=[g for g in validation['convergence'] if max(g['peak_600_N'],g['peak_1200_N'])>=50]
    pending=[g for g in significant if g['relative_peak_difference']>=.05 or g['curve_RMS_over_peak']>=.05]
    report=dict(status=validation['status'],motion=quality,calf=audit,pending_muscle_groups=pending,unidentified_MTP_support=validation['unidentified_plantar_support'])
    (out/'revision_audit.json').write_text(json.dumps(report,indent=2))
    content=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width"><title>Calf moment audit</title><style>body{{max-width:1100px;margin:30px auto;padding:20px;background:#0d1726;color:#edf3fb;font:18px/1.65 system-ui}}a{{color:#8ce2d5}}table{{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:15px}}td,th{{border:1px solid #465e76;padding:8px}}.scroll{{overflow:auto}}strong{{color:#f0b74e}}</style><a href="index.html">Back to viewer</a><h1>Upright jump and calf-force audit</h1><p><strong>This remains a conditional diagnostic model. Whole-body balance passes; individual muscle predictions are not yet validated.</strong></p><h2>What was corrected</h2><p>The prior motion maintained substantial whole-body angular momentum and rotated in flight. It is rejected as a vertical-jump reference. This revision controls angular momentum through actual solved ground contacts, frees the MTP hinges, places forefoot contacts on toe bodies and enforces a circular Coulomb cone with mu=0.8. No muscle force cap was introduced.</p><p>Generic subject: 180 cm, 90 kg. New peak combined vertical GRF: {q['peak_total_vertical_GRF_N']:.0f} N ({q['peak_GRF_bodyweights']:.2f} bodyweights). Takeoff angular momentum: {q['takeoff_angular_momentum_kg_m2_s']:.4f} kg m²/s. Maximum physical thorax tilt in flight: {q['maximum_flight_thorax_tilt_deg']:.2f} degrees. Landing is excluded.</p><h2>Why internal tension can exceed ground force</h2><p>Ground force acts through the COP. Its ankle moment is (COP − ankle) × GRF. Internal muscle moments must balance that moment plus the foot segment inertial/gravity terms. A short muscle moment arm can require a larger internal force. Total GRF is therefore not an internal-force ceiling. This does not establish that this model's assumed COP or muscle paths match a real person.</p><p>At the peak of each modeled calf group, the following quantities are reconstructed from the same physical frame. Calf tension is the scalar sum of soleus and both gastrocnemius elements; it is not a direct measurement of common Achilles tendon force.</p><div class="scroll"><table><tr><th>Side</th><th>Time [s]</th><th>Same-foot Fz [N]</th><th>External lever [cm]</th><th>Net ankle demand [Nm]</th><th>Calf moment [Nm]</th><th>Calf arm [cm]</th><th>Calf sum [N]</th></tr>{''.join(rows)}</table></div><p>Muscle moment arms were additionally checked by central finite differences of native muscle path lengths. Full vectors, opposing muscle moments, passive contributions and finite-difference errors are available in <a href="../contact_jump_scapula/600hz/calf_moment_audit.json">the frame audit</a>.</p><h2>What is still unresolved</h2><p>{len(pending)} muscle groups exceed the declared 5% time-step sensitivity criterion for peak or curve RMS over the common time interval. See <a href="validation.json">all convergence results</a>. Calf peak consistency alone does not validate its anatomical moment arm, COP distribution or passive force law.</p><p>The current foot lacks intrinsic muscle and plantar-fascial support. Instead of forcing their missing moments into extrinsic toe muscles, the MTP support moment is retained as an unidentified internal couple. Toe muscle colors and force readouts are withheld. These components must be modeled before interpreting plantar tissue loads.</p><p>Reaction-cone stability, generic passive tension and the force-sharing criterion still affect antagonist load. Conservation identifies net requirements, not a unique muscle recruitment strategy. No empirical force or motion validation has been claimed.</p><h2>Primary research context</h2><p><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23915826/">Directly measured versus ankle-moment-derived Achilles force during vertical jumps</a> illustrates both internal-force amplification and the limitations of deriving tendon force from ankle moment. <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37787026/">Jump-landing Achilles force estimation</a> examines the role of kinematics, ground force and COP. Neither study supplies a universal force ceiling for this generic model.</p><p><a href="revision_audit.json">Machine-readable revision audit</a> · <a href="method.html">Complete equations and assumptions</a></p></html>'''
    moment=abs(audit['audits'][0]['calf_muscle_moment_Nm'])
    sensitivity=''.join(f'<tr><td>{r*100:.0f}</td><td>{moment/r:.0f}</td></tr>' for r in [.03,.04,.05,.06])
    content=content.replace('<h2>What is still unresolved</h2>',f'<h2>Moment-arm sensitivity</h2><p>Holding the same calf moment ({moment:.1f} Nm) fixed, tension changes as moment / moment arm. This is an algebraic sensitivity illustration, not a second full simulation or a claim that one radius is correct.</p><table><tr><th>Assumed effective calf arm [cm]</th><th>Tension for same moment [N]</th></tr>{sensitivity}</table><p><a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3871454/">Subject-specific Achilles moment-arm measurements</a> show angle, contraction state and measurement-method dependence. A generic short path arm must not be mistaken for a validated personal anatomical value.</p><h2>What is still unresolved</h2>')
    if (out/'foot_force_balance.json').exists():
        foot=json.loads((out/'foot_force_balance.json').read_text());a=foot['audits'][0]
        terms=[('Ground on foot',a['ground_force_N'][2]),('Calf on foot',a['calf_force_vector_N'][2]),('Other muscles on foot',a['other_muscle_force_vector_N'][2]),('Ankle joint on foot',a['proximal_ankle_reaction_on_foot_N'][2]),('Foot weight',a['weight_N'][2])]
        tab=''.join(f'<tr><td>{name}</td><td>{force:+.1f}</td></tr>' for name,force in terms)
        section=f'<h2>Where is the opposing force?</h2><p>Both force and moment equations must hold. For the right foot at {a["time_s"]:.3f} s, all values below are vertical components of vectors acting ON the complete foot; positive is upward. The calf scalar tension sum is not its vertical force component.</p><table><tr><th>Force on complete foot</th><th>Vertical component [N]</th></tr>{tab}</table><p>The force sum equals the mass-weighted foot acceleration term ({a["mass_times_COM_acceleration_N"][2]:.6f} N). Full 3D residual norm: {a["force_balance_error_N"]:.2g} N. Previously saved ankle reaction magnitude: {a["proximal_reaction_magnitude_N"]:.0f} N. Equal and opposite joint and muscle forces act on the other body attachments and cancel when the whole body is considered.</p><p><strong>The ideal ankle permits large reaction forces.</strong> Satisfying its force equation does not establish that the contact geometry, passive tensions or force-sharing selection are realistic. A large muscle force is not justified by moment balance alone.</p><p><a href="foot_force_balance.json">Full saved-reaction free-body audit</a> · <a href="https://opensimconfluence.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/OpenSim/pages/53089600/Joint+Reactions+Analysis">OpenSim joint reaction documentation</a></p>'
        content=content.replace('<h2>What is still unresolved</h2>',section+'<h2>What is still unresolved</h2>')
    (out/'calf_audit.html').write_text(content,encoding='utf-8')
    readme=ROOT/'README.md';s=readme.read_text(encoding='utf-8');old=s.index('---');head=f'''# Upright jump diagnostic revision — 2026-11-19

뷰어: `open_jump_contact_lab.cmd` / 새 영상: `results/jump_contact_visualization/jump_tension_upright_v3.mp4` / 재현: `rebuild_jump_contact.cmd`.

- 이전 공중 회전 모션은 수직 점프 기준으로 부적합하여 제외했습니다. 실제 몸통 비행 기울기 최대 {q['maximum_flight_thorax_tilt_deg']:.2f}°, 이륙 각운동량 {q['takeoff_angular_momentum_kg_m2_s']:.4f} kg·m²/s를 별도 검사합니다.
- 180 cm / 90 kg. 양발 합산 최대 지면 반력 {q['peak_total_vertical_GRF_N']:.0f} N. 독립 MTP 관절과 발당 6개 접촉점, 원형 마찰 원뿔 안쪽 16면 근사를 사용합니다. 착지는 계산하지 않습니다.
- 438개 근육 요소와 별도 견갑 접촉 반력. 근력 상한을 두지 않으며, 근육 경로와 순 관절 모멘트로 하나의 조건부 장력 해를 구합니다.
- 종아리 감사 보고서: `results/jump_contact_visualization/calf_audit.html`. 지면 반력, COP, 발목 모멘트, 근육 지렛팔, 수동 장력을 같은 시각에서 대조합니다.
- **전신 보존·접촉 검사는 통과하지만 일부 근육 장력의 시간 간격 민감도는 아직 해결되지 않았습니다. 실제 인체의 근육 부하 예측 정확도를 주장하지 않습니다.** 이전 문서의 전체 근군 수렴 통과 문구는 현재 결과에 적용하지 않습니다.
- 내재근·족저근막이 빠진 MTP 지지 모멘트는 미확정 내부 관절 모멘트로 남깁니다. 발가락 근육의 색과 수치 표시는 보류합니다. 이를 임의 근육 힘으로 메우지 않습니다.
- 전신 전면 사선/후면, 8개 시간 컨투어, 검정→빨강 관절 뼈 표면. 1080×1920, 하단 384 px 공백. 3회 반복은 동일 계산의 0.5배속 재생입니다.

가정과 수치 검사: `results/jump_contact_visualization/method.html`, `validation.json`, `revision_audit.json`.

''';readme.write_text(head+s[old:],encoding='utf-8')
    print('REVISION_DOCUMENTED',len(pending),'sensitive muscle groups')

if __name__=='__main__':main()
